      ],
      "explanation": "The exponent \\(2y\\) suggests viewing the given power as a square:\n\\[\n(10^y)^2=10^{2y}=25.\n\\]\nA positive base raised to a real exponent is positive, so \\(10^y>0\\). Consequently, \\(10^y=5\\); the negative square root cannot apply. Opposite exponents give reciprocal values, so\n\\[\n10^{-y}=\\frac1{10^y}=\\frac15.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(\\dfrac15\\), choice E.",
      "id": "positive-square-and-reciprocal",
